        "original_id": "8cb270bb-580f-5385-9b90-49a5a710e97c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: New York State, Quebec, Catskill Mountains, Lake Huron, New England\n- Concepts: Queenston Delta, Taconic orogeny\n\nFacts:\n- The Taconic orogeny was a mountain-building period that ended 440 million years ago.\n- The Taconic orogeny affected most of modern-day New England.\n- The Queenston Delta wedge is thickest in a band running from New York State to Quebec.\n- The Queenston Delta wedge extends from the Catskill Mountains to Lake Huron.",
